Let's break down how to read a CSV file in JavaScript.

**Understanding the Challenge**

JavaScript, running primarily in web browsers, doesn't directly have built-in tools to access your computer's file system for security reasons. This means we'll need a bit of help:

* **File Input:** We'll use an HTML `<input type="file">` element to allow the user to select a CSV file from their computer.
* **FileReader API:**  This powerful JavaScript API allows us to read the contents of files selected by the user.

**The Code**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>CSV Reader</title>
</head>
<body>

<h1>CSV Reader</h1>

<input type="file" id="csvFileInput" accept=".csv">

<pre id="csvOutput"></pre>

<script>
  const fileInput = document.getElementById('csvFileInput');
  const outputArea = document.getElementById('csvOutput');

  fileInput.addEventListener('change', (event) => {
    const file = event.target.files[0];

    const reader = new FileReader();

    reader.onload = (event) => {
      const csvData = event.target.result;
      // Process the CSV data here
      outputArea.textContent = csvData; 
    };

    reader.readAsText(file);
  });
</script>

</body>
</html>
